lling point of the game it's not  I made a talking point it's not a major  Pro or condo this is why I think game  reviews are pretty much always  subjective because you are deciding  which of the things presented to you is  important and which isn't and someone  else who's writing the review might  disagree with that opinion so basically  I usually try to write bullet points for  each thing that I think is really  important whether it's a prior record  and then I flush those out into a larger  thing I elaborate on those points I give  examples for the  written version for the video version we  don't need to give examples because you  can show that with gameplay and we'll  get to that in the gameplay recording  part but next to picking what is  particularly important to talk about  it's really important that every single  sentence that you write evaluates the  game in some way a lot of people make  the mistake of writing a sentence that  just says this game does this where you  should be saying this game does this and  this is good or bad because the next  option would be to send it to an editor  if you have one but if you don't to  really thoroughly edit stuff yourself  cut out everything that isn't important  and stick to a word limit if you don't  have someone else giving you one so that  you're not just rambling for a really  really long time so I've sent the script  off to Dan who's the editor and while he  works on the script I will stop writing  the full review because the script is  more important we need to record  gameplay and vo for the video editors  and I won't decide the school that I'm  going to give the game until I have my  full review written so I can kind of  figure out what it riggins like rather  than what I just have in my head that  Noma doesn't just appear out of nowhere  but right now it is 10:00 p.m. so I'm  going to go home and we'll have Dan's  edits tomorrow I'll start on the written  review and I'll start recording gameplay  so at this point you're ready to record  gameplay based off of what is in the  script so I record gameplay after  writing the script not beforehand we  have out gameplay recording setup in  here what I would do is go through my  script and highlight plots of text and  then search for those in the game based  on what I have played some games you  have to start over some games  conveniently have checkpoints so the  script is written with what I know I can  recall it in mind so that when I am  recording the gameplay I know how easy  it'll be to match up to the script but  basically I attach files to the script  so that the editors know exactly what  I'm referring to when they are making  the video so I now have my approved  edits back from Dan basically Dan just  edit spots of the script which we have  here right now this is all been approved  and I have agreed with Dan's edits so we  jump into the vo booth this is a fully  sub / firm which is actually very hot  and I have my script ready to go I will  have someone listening when I'm  recording it to make sure that there  aren't any ones that I stumble on  without realizing make sure the things I  say a consistent because it's really  easy to just say the wrong thing  accidentally and not realize when you're  in front of the camera all recording vo  so let's do it so my review is almost  written have recorded and play a  recorded vo so the video team can start  editing now I have to finish the full  review and work on the score and the  pros and cons which again part of i GN  specific style guide but I will need to  do those to be edited into the video and  wrap the whole thing up so I have  finished writing my full review I think  I've already mentioned most of the  important stuff since we don't use  headers I also make sure to link things  together so I have linking sentences  which you wouldn't normally have in the  video version of the review and we  actually recently got rid of word counts  but I think this one is about 800 